(" determined immediately before the discharge",""),
("strictly limited","limited"),
("To claim the insolvency or bankruptcy exclusions, taxpayers must file Form 982, titled Reduction of Tax Attributes Due to Discharge of Indebtedness. Excluded amounts reported on Form 982 generally require reducing specific tax attributes as detailed in the statutory rules.","Excluded amounts are reported on Form 982, Reduction of Tax Attributes Due to Discharge of Indebtedness, and generally require reducing tax attributes (IRS Topic 431)."),
("State tax treatment of student loan forgiveness may differ from federal tax provisions. \n\n Borrowers should check their state's rules.","State tax treatment of student loan forgiveness may differ from federal tax treatment. Check your state's rules."),
